[94mEAT(1)                      General Commands Manual                     EAT(1)[m

[94mNAME[m
       eat - a syntax-highlighting cat

[94mSYNOPSIS[m
       eat [OPTIONS] [FILE]...

[94mDESCRIPTION[m
       eat prints the highlighted contents of FILEs. See also [33mcat(1)[m and
       [33mprintf(3p)[m for related tools.

[94mOPTIONS[m
       -A, [94m--show-all[m
              Show non-printable characters.

       -l, [94m--language[m <LANG>
              Override syntax detection.

       -p, [94m--plain[m
              Disable highlighting and decorations.

[94mENVIRONMENT VARIABLES[m
       EAT_PAGER
              The pager binary; falls back to [96m$PAGER[m, then less.

[94mEXAMPLES[m
       eat -l rust src/main.rs
       printf [91m'hello'[m | eat -l shellscript

[94mSEE ALSO[m
       [33mbat(1)[m, [33mcat(1)[m, [33mless(1)[m

